From 630d1031add429b5714ac52a5d6383944d949aa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:57:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license_files to cover the vendored Eigen licence

setup.cfg's explicit license_files list only names LICENSE.txt, so
setuptools' default LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING* glob never applies here and a
dropped-in COPYING.eigen is silently ignored. riskfolio.external.functions
links Eigen 3.4.0, vendored at lib/eigen-3.4.0 without its licence reaching
dist-info/licenses on any architecture's wheel, not just riscv64's.

Widening the list to also name COPYING.eigen lets it reach
dist-info/licenses/ once the build stages it at the project root (copied
from lib/eigen-3.4.0/COPYING.MPL2, already vendored alongside Eigen's own
sources), with no other packaging change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every riskfolio-lib wheel on PyPI regardless of architecture, so this needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.cfg | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index ef9e2d1..ce34374 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -1,2 +1,4 @@
 [metadata]
-license_files = LICENSE.txt
+license_files =
+	LICENSE.txt
+	COPYING.eigen
-- 
2.43.0

